==English==
{{swp}}

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:techere|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|techere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|teach|-er|id2=agent noun}}. More at {{m|en|teach}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|en|non-rhotic}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈtiː.t͡ʃəː/|[ˈtʰɪi̯.t͡ʃəː]|a=RP}}
*** {{audio|en|En-uk-teacher.ogg|a=UK}}
*** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-teacher.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{a|en|rhotic}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈti.t͡ʃɚ/|[ˈtʰɪi̯.t͡ʃɚ]|~|[ˈtʰɪi̯.t͡ʃɹ̩]|a=GA,[[w:Standard Canadian English|Standard Canadian]]}}
*** {{audio|en|en-us-teacher.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːtʃə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{hyph|en|tea|cher}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A person who [[teach]]es, especially one employed in a [[school]]; preceptor.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2013-07-19|author=[http://www.theguardian.com/profile/marktran Mark Tran]
|volume=189|issue=6|page=1|magazine=w:The Guardian Weekly
|title=Denied an education by war
|url=http://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2013/jul/12/war-denying-children-education
|passage=One particularly damaging, but often ignored, effect of conflict on education is the proliferation of attacks on schools{{...}}as children, '''teachers''' or school buildings become the targets of attacks. Parents fear sending their children to school. Girls are particularly vulnerable to sexual violence.}}
# The [[index finger]]; the [[forefinger]].
# An [[indication]]; a [[lesson]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Steve LeVine|title= Trump Speech to Congress: The Message Was Trumpian, But The Tone Was Decidedly Not|work=w:Quartz|url=https://qz.com/921758/trump-speech-to-congress-the-message-was-trumpian-but-the-tone-was-decidedly-not/|date=28 February 2017|passage=But if the last two years are a '''teacher''', look for the bombastic tweets to resume before sunrise.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250709230258/https://qz.com/921758/trump-speech-to-congress-the-message-was-trumpian-but-the-tone-was-decidedly-not|archivedate=9 July 2025}}
# {{lb|en|Mormonism}} The second highest office in the [[w:Aaronic priesthood|Aaronic priesthood]], held by priesthood holders of at least the age of 14.

====Synonyms====
