worker.content:
==English==

===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:worchere<alt:werkere, worchere>|tree=+}}
{{inh+|en|enm|worchere}}, {{m|enm|werkere}}, equivalent to {{af|en|work|-er|id2=agent noun}}. Displaced the older term {{m|en|wright}}, from {{cog|ang|wyrhta}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɜː.kə/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈwɝ.kɚ/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-worker.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|En-uk-worker.ogg|a=UK}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɜː(ɹ)kə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[work#Verb|works]]: a [[person]] who [[perform]]s [[labor#Noun|labor]] for a [[living#Noun|living]]; traditionally, especially, [[manual#Adjective|manual]] labor.
#: {{hypo|en|laborer|labourer|;|blue-collar worker|white-collar worker|;|drone|drudge}}
#: {{cot|en|boss|manager|employer<qq:sometimes [[coinstantial]]>}}
#: {{nearsyn|en|employee}}
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Psalms|37|1|url=https://archive.org/stream/Bible1611/Binder1#page/n664/mode/1up|passage=Fret not thy ſelfe becauſe of euill doers, neither bee thou enuious againſt the '''workers''' of iniquitie.}}
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1986
|author=w:Janice G. Raymond
|title=A Passion for Friends: Toward a Philosophy of Female Affection
|url=https://archive.org/details/passionforfriend0000raym/
|location=[[Boston]]
|publisher=w:Beacon Press
|ISBN=0-8070-6724-5
|LCCN=85-47942
|OCLC=803087560
|page=124
|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/passionforfriend0000raym/page/124/
|text=Writer Ta Chen, in a statistical study of industrial labor in China in 1933, recorded that 66.6 percent of the total number of '''workers''' in the four main industrial regions of Kwangtung were women. In Shun-te, 81.2 percent of the labor force were women.}}
