==English==
{{wp}}
[[File:Algo clasico (5106726351).jpg|thumb|right|250px|[[yellow cab|Yellow cab]] taxis in [[New York City]], the usual image of taxis in American culture]]
[[File:Two black cabs with Big Ben in the background.jpg|thumb|right|250px|[[black cab|Black cab]] taxis in [[London]], the usual image of taxis in British culture]]
[[File:Taxiing Airplanes at DXB on 13 November 2007.jpg|thumb|right|250px|A line of airplanes taxiing on the runway at DXB in [[Dubai]] in the [[UAE]], 2007.]]
[[File:2. Minibus taxi in Maboneng, Johannesburg, South Africa.jpg|thumb|right|250px|A shared taxi ("taxi") waiting for more passengers to leave in [[Johannesburg]], South Africa <small>(2017)</small>]]

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*teh₂g-|id=touch}}
Shortened from {{m|en|taximeter cab}}, {{m|en|taximeter||automatic meter that records distance and fare}} from {{der|en|fr|taximètre}}, from {{der|en|de|Taxameter}} (whence also {{cog|en|taxameter}}), coined from {{der|en|la-med|taxa||tax, charge}}.<ref>{{R:Etymonline}}</ref> More at {{m|en|tax}}, {{m|en|task}}.

The aviation sense originally derived from a slang term for training aircraft used for practicing ground operations, which were said to drive around the airfield like a taxicab, and subsequently applied to all aircraft ground movements.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtæksi/|a=RP,GA,AU}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-taxi.ogg|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtaksɪj/|a=SSB}}
** {{audio|en|En-uk-a taxi.ogg|a=SSB}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtakse/|/ˈtaksɪ/|/ˈtaksi/|a=Scotland}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛksi/|a=NZ}}
* {{rhymes|en|æksi|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|s|es}}

# A [[vehicle]], usually a [[car]], that may be [[hire]]d for single [[journey]]s by members of the public, [[particularly]] one with an [[automated]] [[meter]] to [[calculate]] the [[fare]].
#: {{ux|en|I cabbed a package downtown in my father's '''taxi'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1932|year_published=1965|author=w:Delos W. Lovelace|title=[[w:King Kong (1933 film)|King Kong]]|page=12|passage="'''Taxi'''," he called. And when one pulled up to the curb with screeching brakes he ordered, "The nearest restaurant."}}
#* '''2007 August 24''', Graham Linehan, ''{{w|The IT Crowd}}'', Season 2, Episode 1:
#*: [''Sobbing uncontrollably''] I thought I could make it work between us because you looked a bit like a man.<br>'''TAXI'''!
# {{lb|en|aviation|slang|obsolete}} An aircraft used for practicing ground manoeuvres.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1912|title=Flight: The Aircraft Engineer
|text=Capt. Dawes and Bellairs were out with the Deperdussin '''taxi''', and also with the brevet machine, rolling.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914|title=Aeroplane and Commercial Aviation News
|text=... some similar untidy pile of what had been a school biplane is recorded to have acted the part of red rag to the bull of a "'''taxi'''" monoplane , which despite its driver's efforts insisted on charging and trampling on the battered fragments.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|title=The Aeroplane
|text=Mr. E. B. Bauman (new pupil) joined school and had first lesson on No. 2 '''taxi'''.}}
# {{lb|en|aviation|uncountable|countable}} The movement of an [[aircraft]] across an [[airport]]'s surface under its own power; a phase of aircraft operation involving this movement.
#: {{ux|en|During '''taxi''', the flaps and slats are extended and the second engine (if not already running) is started.}}
#: {{ux|en|Seat belts must be kept fastened during '''taxi''', takeoff, turbulence, and landing.}}
# {{lb|en|South Africa|Iran}} {{synonym of|en|shared taxi}}.

====Synonyms====
