==English==
[[File:Anaconda jaune 34.JPG|thumb|[[yellow anaconda|Yellow anaconda]] ({{taxlink|Eunectes notaeus|species}})]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|noun: the animal}} {{alt|en|snek||internet slang|childish|jocular}}

===Etymology===
{{dercat|en|gem-pro|inh=1}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:snake|tree=++}}
From {{inh|en|enm|snake}}, from {{inh|en|ang|snaca|t=snake, serpent, reptile}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*snakō|t=slider, snake}}, from {{m|gmw-pro|*snakan|t=to creep, slide}}, related to {{cog|goh|snahhan|t=to sneak, slide}}. Compare also {{cog|gem-pro|*snēkô|t=creeper, crawler}}.

Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|Snake}}, {{m|nds-de|Snaak|t=snake}}, dialectal {{cog|de|Schnake|t=adder}}, {{cog|da|snog|t=grass snake}}, {{cog|sv|snok|t=grass snake}}, {{cog|nn|snåk|t=viper, adder}}, {{cog|fo|snákur|t=grass snake}}, {{cog|is|snákur|t=snake}}.

