===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q2102}} Any of the suborder {{taxfmt|Serpentes|suborder}} of [[legless]] [[reptile]]s with elongated bodies and fork-shaped tongues.
#: {{syn|en|Joe Blake|serpent}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1892|author=w:Oscar Wilde|title=w:A House of Pomegranates|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=6sUVAAAAYAAJ|passage=The man writhed like a trampled '''snake''', and a red foam bubbled from his lips.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1950|month=April|author=Timothy H. Cobb|title=The Kenya-Uganda Railway|journal=Railway Magazine|page=263|text=After dark the train is a lighted '''snake''', as, even when the passengers' lights are out, each carriage has a side-light in the middle just under the eaves.}}
# {{senseid|en|deceitful person}} {{lb|en|figurative}} A person who acts deceitfully for personal or social gain; a [[treacherous]] person.
#: {{hyper|en|jerk<id:Q193607>|<|person#Noun|Thesaurus:jerk}}
#: {{hypo|en|snake in the grass#Noun}}
#: {{nearsyn|en|rat#Noun|Thesaurus:betrayer}}
#* {{RQ:Dickens Nicholas Nickleby|passage=Mrs. Kenwigs was horror-stricken to think that she should ever have nourished in her bosom such a '''snake''', adder, viper, serpent, and base crocodile, as Henrietta Petowker.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2021|author=Peter McKenna|title={{w|Kin (Irish TV series)|Kin}}|season=1|number=2|time=5:51|role=Frank Kinsella|actor=w:Aidan Gillen|passage=Well, if it was Moore, he's a fucking '''snake'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=Jon Henley|title=Old master painting looted by Nazis spotted in Argentinian property listing|date=2025-08-26|url=https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/26/old-master-painting-giuseppe-ghislandi-looted-by-nazis-argentina-property-listing|passage={{q-g|Friedrich}} Kadgien—described by US interrogators as “not a true Nazi” but “a '''snake''' of the lowest sort”—subsequently left Switzerland for Brazil then Argentina, the paper said, where he started a company and a family and died in 1978, aged 71.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250905054416/https://www.theguardian.com/world/2025/aug/26/old-master-painting-giuseppe-ghislandi-looted-by-nazis-argentina-property-listing}}
# A [[tool]] for unclogging [[plumbing]].
#: {{syn|en|auger|plumber's snake}}
# A tool to aid [[cable]] pulling.
#: {{syn|en|wirepuller}}
# {{lb|en|UK|Australia}} A flavoured [[jube]] ([[confectionary]]) in the shape of a snake.
# {{lb|en|slang}} [[trouser snake|Trouser snake]]; the [[penis]].
#: {{syn|en|trouser snake}}
# {{lb|en|maths}} A series of [[Bézier curve]]s.
# {{lb|en|cartomancy}} The seventh [[Lenormand]] card.
# {{lb|en|AAVE|MLE|MTE}} An [[informer]]; a [[rat]].
#: {{syn|en|Thesaurus:informant}}
#: {{ux|en|Gem’s a '''snake''' for Kamale, man.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|date=2017-04-07|title=War Dub|artist=Little T (Josh Tate)|text=Yo, bare people and the '''snakes''', yeah, they're just grass / Next minute you're the mate, yeah / Next day stab in the back}}
# {{lb|en|skateboarding|slang}} A [[person]] who [[interfere]]s with another's [[run]] or who takes their run [[out of turn]].
# {{lb|en|finance|historical}} {{ellipsis of|en|snake in the tunnel}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=W. Bonefeld|title=The Politics of Europe: Monetary Union and Class|page=69
|passage=The '''snake''' failed to provide an anchor for currency stability and, through it, disinflation.}}
