===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=Q8331|:inh|enm:fox<id:Q8331>|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|fox}}, from {{inh|en|ang|fox|t=fox}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*fuhs}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*fuhsaz|t=fox}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*púḱsos|t=the tailed one}}, possibly from {{m|ine-pro|*puḱ-|t=tail}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|yol|vox}}, {{m|yol|voxe|t=fox}}, {{cog|frr|foos|t=fox}}, {{cog|stq|Foaks|t=fox}}, {{cog|fy|foks|t=fox}}, {{cog|gsw|Fuchs}}, {{m|gsw|Fugs}}, {{m|gsw|fuksch}}, {{m|gsw|fuks}}, {{m|gsw|fòcks}}, {{m|gsw|vucks|t=fox}}, {{cog|bar|Fuchs}}, {{m|bar|vucs}}, {{m|bar|vuks|t=fox}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|Fuss|t=fox}}, {{cog|cim|buks}}, {{m|bar|vuks|t=fox}}, {{cog|nl|vos|t=fox}}, {{cog|de|Fuchs|t=fox}}, {{cog|nds|Voss|t=fox}}, {{cog|lb|Fuuss|t=fox}}, {{cog|wym|füks|t=fox}}, {{cog|yi|פֿוקס|t=fox}}, {{cog|nrn|fúa|t=she-fox}}, {{cog|got|𐍆𐌰𐌿𐌷𐍉|t=fox}}; also {{cog|bg,ru,uk|пух|t=down, fluff}}, {{cog|pl|puch|t=down, fluff; snow}}, {{cog|sa|पुच्छ|tr=púccha|t=tail; hind-part}} (whence {{cog|bn|পুচ্ছ|t=tail}}, {{cog|hi|पूँछ}}, {{m|hi|पूंछ|t=tail; rear of an object}}, {{cog|pi|puccha|t=tail}}, {{cog|pa|ਪੂਛ|t=tail}}).
{{col-bottom}}

Philosophical sense from the 1953 essay ''{{w|The Hedgehog and the Fox}}'' by {{w|Isaiah Berlin}}. Military aviation sense from the pre-NATO {{w|Allied_military_phonetic_spelling_alphabets#United_States_military_spelling_alphabets|military spelling alphabet}} where [[Fox]] represented ''F'' and was short for 'to fire'.<ref>{{cite-book|en|url=https://archive.org/details/warslangfighting00dick/page/271/mode/1up?q=fox.+To+fire|title=War slang|author=Paul Dickson|1994|page=271}}</ref>

