#* {{RQ:Eddison Worm|page=24|passage=As for thee, false friend, subtle '''fox''', unfaithful servant, this long time am I grown weary of thee slinking up and down my palace devising darkly things I know not: thou, that art nought akin to Witchland, but an outlander, a Goblin exile, a serpent warmed in my bosom to my hurt.}}
