#* {{quote-book|en|year=1908| title=Letter to his fianceé Clementine|author=Winston Churchill| page=| passage='Filled with old doddering peers, '''cute''' financial magnates, clever wirepullers, big brewers with bulbous noses. All the enemies of progress are there — weaklings, sleek, slug, comfortable, self-important individuals.}}
