===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|:inh|enm:flor<id:floor>}}
{{root|en|ine-pro|*pleh₂-}}
{{inh+|en|enm|floor}}, {{m|enm|floour}}, {{m|enm|flor}}, {{m|enm|flore}}, {{m|enm|flour}}, {{m|enm|flur}}, {{m|enm|vlor}}, from {{inh|en|ang|flōr|t=floor, pavement; deck; gangplank}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*flōr}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*flōraz|t=ground; floor}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*pleh₂ros|t=floor}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*pleh₂-|t=flat}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|flair}}, {{m|sco|fluir|t=floor}}, {{cog|stq|Floor|t=floor}}, {{cog|nl|vloer|t=floor}}, {{cog|de|Flur|t=corridor, hall, hallway, stairwell}}, {{cog|li|Vlǫǫr|t=floor}}, {{cog|nds|Floor|t=hallway or entrance to a house}}, {{cog|lb|Flouer|t=countryside, farmland}}; also {{cog|br,kw|leur|t=floor, ground, surface}}, {{cog|ga|lár|t=floor, ground}}, {{cog|gd|làr|t=earth, floor, ground}}, {{cog|gv|laare|t=bottom, deck, floor; level, storey}}, {{cog|cy|llawr|t=floor, ground}}, {{cog|la|plānus|t=even, flat, level}}, {{cog|el|απαλάμη}}, {{m|el|παλάμη|t=hand, palm}}, {{cog|sq|pëllëmbë|t=palm}}, {{cog|ltg|pluons|t=thin}}, {{cog|lv|plāns|t=thin}}, {{cog|lt|plonas|t=fine, slender, thin}}, {{cog|be,mk,ru,uk|по́ле|t=field}}, {{cog|bg|поле́|t=field}}, {{cog|cs,pl,sk|pole|t=field}}, {{cog|sh|по̏ље}}, {{m|sh|pȍlje|t=field}}, {{cog|sl|polje|t=field}}, {{cog|hit|𒁄𒄭𒅖|tr=palḫis|t=broad, wide}}. Related to ''[[flat]]''.
