# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## To put on clothes.
##: {{synonyms|en|get dressed}}
##: {{antonyms|en|disrobe|[[get#Verb|get]] [[undressed#Adjective|undressed]]|strip|undress}}
##: {{ux|en|I rose and '''dressed''' before daybreak.&emsp;&emsp;&emsp; It’s very cold out. '''Dress''' warm.}}
### {{lb|en|specifically}} To attire oneself for a particular (especially formal) occasion, or in a fashionable manner.
###: {{ux|en|They returned home early to '''dress''' for dinner.}}
###* {{RQ:Richardson Pamela|volume=III|chapter=Letter XXX|page=184|passage=The three Gentlemen rode out, and returned juſt Time enough to '''dreſs''' for dinner.}}
###* {{RQ:Trollope Belton Estate|volume=I|chapter=Will Belton|page=62|passage="We'd better get ready for dinner now. I always '''dress''', because papa likes to see it." This she said as a hint to her cousin that he would be expected to change his coat, for her father would have been annoyed had his guest sat down to dinner without such ceremony.}}
###* {{RQ:Woolf Waves|page=85|passage=She has not '''dressed''', because she despises the futility of London.}}
## Of a thing: to [[attain]] a certain [[condition#Noun|condition]] after [[undergo]]ing some [[process#Noun|process]] or [[treatment]] to fit or prepare it for use.
## {{lb|en|euphemistic|chiefly in the [[tailoring#Noun|tailoring]] context}} To allow one's [[penis]] to [[fall#Verb|fall]] to one [[side#Noun|side]] or the other within one's [[trousers]]. {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
##: {{ux|en|While measuring him for his trousers, the tailor asked him if he '''dressed''' to the left or the right.}}
## {{lb|en|slang}} {{ellipsis of|en|cross-dress}}.
## {{lb|en|[[butchering#Noun|butchering]]}} Of an animal carcass: to have a certain [[quantity]] or [[weight#Noun|weight]] after [[removal]] of the internal organs and [[skin#Noun|skin]]; also, to have a certain [[appearance]] after being cut up and prepared for cooking.
## {{lb|en|military|sometimes|imperative as a [[drill#Noun|drill]] [[command#Noun|command]]}} Of soldiers or troops: to arrange into proper formation; especially, to [[form#Verb|form]] into straight lines and at a proper distance from each other.
##: {{ux|en|Right, '''dress'''!|lit=Form a straight line, and align yourself to the right!}}
## {{lb|en|sports}} Of a [[sportsperson]]: to [[put on]] the [[uniform#Noun|uniform]] and have the [[equipment]] [[need#Verb|needed]] to [[play#Verb|play]] a [[sport#Noun|sport]].
##: {{ux|en|Due to a left ankle sprain, the basketball player did not '''dress''' for the game against Indiana.}}

