===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}
[[File:1817-walking-dress-La-Belle-Assemblee.jpg|thumb|A 19th-[[century]] [[illustration]] of a [[woman#Noun|woman]] [[wear#Verb|wearing]] a dress ''(sense 1.1)''.]]

# {{lb|en|countable}}
## {{senseid|en|Q200539}}{{lb|en|clothing}} An [[item#Noun|item]] of [[clothing#Noun|clothing]] (usually [[wear#Verb|worn]] by a [[woman#Noun|woman]] or [[young#Adjective|young]] [[girl#Noun|girl]]) which both [[cover#Verb|covers]] the [[upper#Adjective|upper]] [[part#Noun|part]] of the [[body]] and includes a [[skirt#Noun|skirt]] [[below#Preposition|below]] the [[waist#Noun|waist]].
##: {{syn|en|frock}}
##: {{ux|en|Amy and Mary looked very pretty in their '''dresses'''.}}
##* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=Dangerous Lady|page=36|passage=She looked cool in a grey tailored cotton '''dress''' with a terracotta scarf and shoes and her hair a black silk helmet.}}
## {{lb|en|archaic|_|outside of|_|India}} An item of [[outer#Adjective|outer]] clothing or [[set#Noun|set]] of such [[clothes]] (worn by [[person#Noun|people]] of all [[sex#Noun|sexes]]) which is generally [[decorative#Adjective|decorative]] and [[appropriate#Adjective|appropriate]] for a [[particular#Adjective|particular]] [[occasion#Noun|occasion]], [[profession]], etc.
##* {{RQ:Goldsmith She Stoops to Conquer|page=23|passage=I have been thinking, George, of changing our travelling '''dreſſes''' in the morning. I am grown confoundedly aſhamed of mine.}}
##* {{RQ:Ruskin Political Economy of Art|page=74|passage=No good historical painting ever yet existed, or ever can exist, where the '''dresses''' of the people of the time are not beautiful: {{...}}}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=1918|author=James George Frazer|title=Folk-Lore In The Old Testament|volume=1|page=271|text=[The Creator] fashioned each nation out of clay and painted on each the '''dresses''' they were to wear.}}
### {{lb|en|by extension|India}} Any [[item]] of [[clothing]], or an [[outfit]].
###: {{ux|en|He wore a bright orange '''dress''' to the office yesterday.}}
## {{lb|en|film|television|theater}} {{ellipsis of|en|dress rehearsal}}.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}}
## [[apparel|Apparel]] or clothing, especially when appropriate for a particular occasion, profession, etc.
##: {{ux|en|military '''dress'''}}
##: {{ux|en|He came to the party in formal '''dress'''.}}
##: {{co|en|exquisite taste in '''dress'''}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Antony and Cleopatra|act=II|scene=iv|page=348|column=1|passage=Till I ſhall ſee you in your Souldiers '''dreſſe''', / Which will become you both: Farewell.}}
##* {{RQ:Spectator|issue=14|date=16 March 1711|page=151|passage=[I]t is a kind of acting to go into masquerade, and a man should be able to say or do things proper for the '''dress''' in which he appears. We have now and then rakes in the habit of Roman senators, and grave politicians in the '''dress''' of rakes.}}
##* {{RQ:Dickens Nicholas Nickleby|chapter=Descriptive of a Dinner at Mr. Ralph Nickleby’s, and of the Manner in which the Company Entertained Themselves before Dinner, at Dinner, and after Dinner|page=172|passage=Your black silk frock will be quite '''dress''' enough, my dear, with that pretty little scarf, and a plain band in your hair, and a pair of black silk stock— {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=Justifiably Angry Young Man|page=82|passage=Even in an era when individuality in '''dress''' is a cult, his clothes were noticeable. He was wearing a hard hat of the low round kind favoured by hunting men, and with it a black duffle-coat lined with white.}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} The [[act#Noun|act]] of [[put#Verb|putting]] on clothes, especially [[fashionable]] ones, or for a particular (especially [[formal#Adjective|formal]]) occasion.
## {{lb|en|by extension}}
### The [[external#Adjective|external]] [[covering#Noun|covering]] of an [[animal]] (for example, the [[feather#Noun|feathers]] of a [[bird#Noun|bird]]) or an [[object#Noun|object]].
###* {{RQ:Darwin Descent of Man|volume=II|page=187|passage=When the adults [''i.e.'', birds] of both sexes have a distinct winter and summer plumage, whether or not the male differs from the female, the young resemble the adults of both sexes in their winter '''dress''' or much more rarely in their summer '''dress''', or they resemble the females alone; or the young may have an intermediate character; or again they may differ greatly from the adults in both their seasonal plumages.}}
### The [[appearance]] of an object after it has [[undergo|undergone]] some [[process#Noun|process]] or [[treatment]] to [[fit#Verb|fit]] or [[prepare]] it for [[use#Noun|use]]; [[finish#Noun|finish]].
### {{lb|en|figuratively}} The external appearance of something, especially if [[intend]]ed to [[give#Verb|give]] a [[positive#Adjective|positive]] [[impression]]; [[garb#Noun|garb]], [[guise#Noun|guise]].
###* {{RQ:Jonson Alchemist|scene=i|page=63|passage=Sir, although / VVe may be ſaid to vvant the [[gilt|guilt]], and trappings, / The '''dreſſe''' of ''Honor''; yet vve ſtriue to keepe, / The ſeedes, and the ''Materialls''.}}
###* {{RQ:Boyle Scriptures|pages=163–164|pageref=164|passage={{...}} Eloquence, the '''Dreſs''' of our Thoughts, like the Dreſs of our Bodies, differs not only in ſeveral Regions, but in ſeveral Ages.}}
###* {{RQ:John Gay Wit|page=14|passage=He has indeed reſcued it [''i.e.'', learning] out of the hands of Pedants and Fools, and diſcover'd the true method of making it amiable and lovely to all mankind: In the '''dreſs''' he gives it, 'tis a moſt welcome gueſt at Tea-tables and Aſſemblies, and is reliſh'd and careſſed by the Merchants on the Change; {{...}}}}
### {{lb|en|archaic|historical}} The [[system]] of [[furrow#Noun|furrows]] on the [[face#Noun|face]] of a [[millstone]].
## {{lb|en|obsolete}} The act of [[apply]]ing a [[dressing#Noun|dressing]] to or otherwise [[treat#Verb|treating]] a [[wound#Noun|wound]]; also, the dressing so applied.

