expensive.content:
==English==
[[File:CfShield.JPG|thumb|A cask for transporting [[californium]]-252. {{U|californium-252}} is egregiously '''expensive''', costing ~$27 [[million]] per [[gram]].]]
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)pend-}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|expencive||archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|en|la|*expēnsīvus}}, from {{m|la|expendō||to weigh out (money), to pay out}} (whence {{cog|en|expend}}).<ref>{{R:OED Online|id=5682531809}}</ref> {{surf|en|expense|-ive}}. In the sense of "high-priced" has largely displaced {{m|en|dear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|en|non-weak vowel}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɪkˈspɛn.sɪv/|/ɛkˈspɛn.sɪv/}}
*** {{audio|en|En-us-expensive.ogg|a=US}}
*** {{audio|en|En-uk-expensive.ogg|a=UK|q=female voice}}
*** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Back ache-expensive.wav|a=UK|q=male voice}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɪkˈspɪn.sɪv/|aa=pin-pen}}
* {{a|en|weak vowel}}
** {{IPA|en|/əkˈspɛn.sɪv/}}
** {{IPA|en|/əkˈspɪn.sɪv/|aa=pin-pen}}
* {{hyph|en|ex|pen|sive}}
* {{rhyme|en|ɛnsɪv|s=3}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|more}}

# Having a high [[price]] or [[cost]].
#: {{syn|en|costly|high-priced|pricey|dear|Thesaurus:expensive}}
#: {{ant|en|cheap|inexpensive|low-priced}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2006|author=w:Edwin Black|chapter=The Plan Against Oil|title=Internal Combustion: How Corporations and Governments Addicted the World to Oil and Derailed the Alternatives|location=New York|publisher=w:St. Martin's Press|isbn=9780312359072|page=2|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/internalcombusti00blac/page/2/mode/1up|passage=If successful, Edison and Ford—in 1914—would move society away from the ever more '''expensive''' and then universally known killing hazards of gasoline cars: air and water pollution, noise and noxiousness, constant coughing and the undeniable rise in cancers caused by smoke exhaust particulates.}}
#* {{RQ:Economist|date=Jun 22 2013|title=The G8 summit: T time|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20130709145155/http://www.economist.com/news/finance-and-economics/21579860-g8-pledges-tackle-three-ts-t-time|passage=In Starbucks’s case, the firm has in effect turned the process of making an '''expensive''' cup of coffee into intellectual property.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} Taking a lot of system time or resources.
#: {{ux|en|an unnecessarily '''expensive''' choice of algorithm}}
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} Given to [[expend]]ing a lot of [[money]]; [[profligate]], [[lavish]].
#* {{RQ:Richardson Clarissa|I|letter=IV|''Miſs'' Clarissa Harlowe, ''To Miſs'' Howe|22|{{...}} And that he looked into his own affairs, and underſtood them; That he had, when abroad, been very '''expenſive'''; and contracted a large debt (for he made no ſecret of his affairs); {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Smollett Peregrine Pickle|I|XXV|186|{{...}} thus naturally generous and '''expenſive''', he ſquandered away his money, and made a moſt ſplendid appearance upon the receipt of his quarterly appointment; {{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:Austen Sense and Sensibility|volume=II|chapter=IX|passage='His character is now before you — '''expensive''', dissipated, and worse than both {{...}}'}}
# {{lb|en|cricket}} Having a high [[economy rate]].
#: {{ant|en|economical}}

====Usage notes====
