|passage=When ready for sea we went up to Greenhithe, that their lordships might inspect us, and then to Portsmouth, to take troops to Cork, a pleasant trip; but the troops left us a legacy of "[[mahogany flat]]s," with which their beds were so swarming that we never got them '''under'''.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine|colloquial}} Under [[anesthesia]], especially [[general anesthesia]]; [[sedated]].
#: {{ux|en|Ensure the patient is sufficiently '''under'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1968|author=Agatha Young|chapter=44|title=I Swear by Apollo|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Simon & Schuster|Simon and Schuster]]|page=461|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/iswearbyapollo0000agat/page/461/mode/1up|lccn=68-22975|oclc=442756|passage=To the anesthetist Moynihan said, “Have a look down the hall, will you, and see if the nurse has the bed ready. And leave the doors open when you come back so we can carry him through. Send anybody but the nurse away. Then come back and give us a hand with him. Not that he’s so heavy .&nbsp;.&nbsp;.” And then to Matthew, “He’s so far '''under''' I’m going to wait a bit for the hypo.”}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2007|author=John Likides|chapter=14|title=Infinite Sustain|location=[Philadelphia, Pa.]|publisher=w:Xlibris|page=225|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=3-YGTKdb2UYC&pg=PA225|isbn=978-1-4257-7203-1|passage=She can’t hear us. She’s so far '''under''', that her sensory receptors aren’t working. Her brain regions that regulate waking consciousness and dreaming are shut down. No electrical activity. Only numbness and forgetting.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2009|author=John W. Mangum|chapter=9|title=Full Circle: 360°’s of Life|location=Sonoita, Ariz.|publisher=Running Iron Press|page=83|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/fullcircle360deg0000mang/page/83/mode/1up|isbn=0-9840896-0-8|passage=“Sam, can we see Pop now?” “Sure Kathy, but he’s been sedated and he’s on morphine to control the pain. He won’t be coherent and he might not recognize any of us.” {{...}} “Dad, we’re here. We came to see you.” There was no response. “Pop, we’re here to see you.” “I guess he’s too far '''under''' to recognize us.{{nb...}}”}}
