===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|Q35054}}{{lb|en|countable}} A place ([[building]], [[office]], [[shop]], or [[counter]]) concerned with the business of [[delivering]] [[letter]]s, [[post]] or [[mail]] and [[selling]] [[stamp]]s, etc.
#: {{syn|en|postal outlet|postal service|postal station}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1955|month=June|author=Rev. A. W. V. Mace|title=An Irish Journey—2|journal=Railway Magazine|page=393|text=We were over the border here, into Northern Ireland, and the '''post office''' had a very English atmosphere. It was pleasant, too, much as we enjoyed the hospitality of the Republic, to be buying stamps with the Queen's head on them, and to be posting our cards in a red pillar-box, instead of a green one.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} An organization that delivers letters.
#* {{quote-book
|en
|year=1815
|author=w:Jane Austen
|title=w:Emma
|volume=II
|section=chapter 16
|passage=“The '''post-office''' is a wonderful establishment!” said she.—“The regularity and despatch of it! If one thinks of all that it has to do, and all that it does so well, it is really astonishing!” }}
# {{lb|en|North America|uncountable}} A [[party game]] involving the exchange of [[kiss]]es.
#: {{synonyms|en|postman's knock}}

