excuse me.content:
==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɛksˈkjuːz mi/|/ɪksˈkjuːz mi/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-excuse me.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Phrase===
{{en-head|phr}}

# {{lb|en|North America}} {{n-g|Said as a request to repeat information.}}
# {{lb|en|North America}} {{n-g|Said, as though as a request to repeat information, in order to indicate disbelief or indignation.}}
#: {{usex|en|It was so hot I took off my clothes and sat by the window to cool off.<br />'''Excuse me?'''}}
# {{n-g|Said as a request for an individual's attention.}}
#* '''2016''', [https://web.archive.org/web/20170918070146/https://learningenglish.voanews.com/a/lets-learn-english-lesson-3-i-am-here/3126527.html VOA Learning English] (public domain)
#*: '''Excuse me'''? Anna? Is that you? &mdash; Oh, yes. I am here!
# {{n-g|Said as a request to pass somebody.}}
#: {{ux|en|'''Excuse me''': can I get through please?}}
# [[sorry|Sorry]], {{n-g|as an apology.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=2011|author=w:That Handsome Devil|title=Charlie’s Inferno|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HkSUnEiSVYM|text="'''Excuse me''', sir! There must be someone you've confused me for"}}
# {{lb|en|formal}} {{n-g|Said as an expression of unexpected or early farewell.}}
#: {{usex|en|Oh, '''excuse me''', I hadn't realized how late it was. I need to get home and make dinner.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|request to repeat}} {{l|en|I beg your pardon}}?, [[pardon]]?, [[I'm sorry]]?, [[come again]]?, [[say again]]?, [[sorry]]? {{lb|en|UK|Ireland}}; see also [[Thesaurus:say again]]

====Derived terms====
{{col|en|excuse you|exsqueeze me}}

===See also===
{{col|en|pardon me|your attention please}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|dance}} An [[old-fashioned]] [[type]] of [[dance]] where [[partner]]s are [[constantly]] [[changed]].

