# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[represent]] by means of a map.
#: {{ux|en|This large atlas '''maps''' the whole world in very great detail.}}
#: {{ux|en|Figure 3 '''maps''' the pressure distribution within the human circulatory system.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To create a map of; to examine or survey in order to gather information for a map.
#: {{ux|en|The team is '''mapping''' the route of the new railway line.}}
#: {{ux|en|The space probe is '''mapping''' the Earth's gravitational field.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1956|month=August|title=Mapping Railways from the Air|journal=Railway Magazine|page=499|text=To provide the surveys required for modernisation schemes on British Railways, extensive sections of line in the [[Home Counties]] are to be '''mapped''' from the air. {{...}} The track will be photographed from 1,500 ft. to provide maps of a scale of about 104 ft. to 1 in.}}
#: {{ux|en|This equipment is designed to '''map''' the neurons of the human brain in three dimensions.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|followed by a "[[to]]" phrase}} To have a direct relationship; to [[correspond]].
#: {{ux|en|This doesn't '''map''' to my understanding of how things should work.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=2019|author=Li Huang; James Lambert|title=Another Arrow for the Quiver: A New Methodology for Multilingual Researchers|journal=Journal of Multilingual and Multicultural Development|doi=10.1080/01434632.2019.1596115|page=8|text=Significantly, the aural-oral data does not '''map''' closely to the visual linguistic landscape at NIE.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|followed by a "[[to]]" phrase}} To create a direct relationship to; to create a [[correspondence]] with.
#: {{ux|en|'''Map''' "volume down" to the F2 key.|q=computing}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|transitive|followed by a "[[to]]" phrase}} To act as a [[function]] on something, taking it ''[[to]]'' something else.
#: <math>f</math> '''maps''' <math>A</math> to <math>B</math>, '''mapping''' every <math>a\in A</math> to <math>f(a)\in B</math>.
#: Equivalently: <math> f: A \to B, a\mapsto f(a)</math>
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing}} To [[assign]] a [[drive letter]] to a shared [[folder]].

