#*: At Siena I was '''tabled''' in the house of one Alberto Scipioni
# {{senseid|en|depict}} {{lb|en|obsolete}} To [[delineate]]; to [[represent]], as in a picture; to [[depict]]. {{defdate|17th–19th c.}}
#* '''c. 1607''', {{w|Francis Bacon}}, letter to {{w|Tobie Matthew}}
#*: '''tabled''' and pictured in the chambers of meditation
# {{senseid|en|add to the agenda}} {{lb|en|non-US}} To put on the table of a commission or legislative assembly; to propose for formal [[discussion]] or [[consideration]], to put on the agenda. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|moot<id:bring up for debate>|propose#Verb}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=16 January 2019|author=Heather Stewart; Daniel Boffey|journal=The Guardian
