##: {{ux|en|'''Behind''' the smile was a cruel intention.}}
## {{lb|en|figuratively}} In the past, from the viewpoint of.
##: {{ux|en|All my problems are '''behind''' me.}}
# Less forward or advanced than; [[after]].
#: {{antonyms|en|ahead of}}
## After in physical progress or [[distance]].
##: ''Smith finished the race a lap '''behind''' the others.''
##* {{RQ:Stevenson Treasure Island| passage=About the center, and a good way '''behind''' the rest, Silver and I followed — I tethered by my rope{{nb...}}.}}
## After in developmental progress, score, grade, etc.; inferior to.
