===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*tek-|id=weave}}
{{etymon|en|id=bathroom|:bor|frm:toilette<id:?>}}
From {{der|en|frm|toilette}}, diminutive of {{m|fr|toile||cloth}}, from their use to protect clothing while shaving or arranging hair. From its use as a private room, ''toilet'' came to refer euphemistically to [[lavatories]] and then to its fixtures, beginning in the United States in the late 19th century.

