#* {{quote-book|en|year=1792|author={{w|Charlotte Smith (writer)|Charlotte Smith}}|title=Desmond|publisher=Broadview|year_published=2001|page=373|passage=Never, my dear Bethel, did the most feverish dreams of fiction produce scenes more painful, or more terrific, than the real events to which I have been an '''actor''', since the date of my last letter.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=February 8, 1852|title=Reminiscences|journal=The Daily Union (Washington) |url=https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn82003410/1852-02-08/ed-1/seq-2/|page=2|text=Mr. Clay had been too prominent an '''actor''' in public affairs to allow whig deception and misrepresentation a fair opportunity for successful action.}}
