===Etymology===
From {{der|en|enm|cage}}, from {{der|en|fro|cage}}, from {{der|en|la|cavea}}. {{doublet|en|cadge|cavea}} and related to {{m|en|jail}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/keɪd͡ʒ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-cage.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|eɪdʒ|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# An [[enclosure]] made of [[spaced]] [[bar]]s, normally to hold animals while providing some ventilation.
#: {{ux|en|We keep a bird in a '''cage'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|The tigers are in a '''cage''' to protect the public.}}
#: {{ux|en|The most dangerous prisoners are locked away in a '''cage'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Henry 4-2|act=IV|scene=ii|lines=48–49|passage=For his father had / never a house but the '''cage'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1642
|author=w:Richard Lovelace|title=w:To Althea, from Prison|others=stanza 4|lines=1–2
|passage=Stone walls do not a prison make, / Nor iron bars a '''cage'''.}}
# The [[passenger]] [[compartment]] of a [[lift]].
# {{lb|en|hockey|water polo}} The [[goal]].
# {{short for|en|roll cage}}{{ngd|, a [[protective]] [[structure]] around the [[passenger]] [[compartment]] of a [[vehicle]].}}
# {{lb|en|by extension|US|slang}} {{synonym of|en|automobile}}.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Something that hinders freedom.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=17 Dec 89|volume=17|number=23|journal=Gay Community News|page=9|author=Nan Donald|title=Broken Hearts, Messed Up Families, And New Beginnings|text=Schwartz examines with dignity and tenderness the battles within and without of {{...}} families, created and biological, and the '''cages''' and freedom they can provide.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|artist=Arcade Fire|title=My Body Is a Cage|album=Neon Bible|author=Jeremy Gara; Régine Chassagne|year=2007|passage=My body is a '''cage''' / That keeps me from dancing with the one I love / But my mind holds the key}}
# {{lb|en|slang}} A [[prison]] or [[prison cell]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=14 Dec 85|volume=13|number=22|journal=Gay Community News|page=4|author=Robyn Shawnee Jackson|title=Kouuntry And Kitten|text=The 'out of the closet' lesbians and gay men here in the Iowa '''Cages''' are harassed and discriminated daily by oppressive pigs, believe me, I know, as a lesbian I've experienced it first hand and seen my fellow lesbian and gay friends oppressed to where I'm ready to explode.}}
# {{lb|en|athletics}} The area from which competitors throw a [[discus]] or [[hammer]].
# An outer framework of timber, enclosing something within it.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1842|year_published=1851|author=w:Joseph Gwilt|title=An Encyclopædia of Architecture, Historical, Theoretical, and Practical
|chapter=A Glossary of Terms Used by Architects
|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=HVZDAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA941|edition=2nd
|publisher=Longman, Brown, Green, and Longmans|location=London|page=941
|passage='''Cage''', in carpentry, is an outer work of timber inclosing another within it.  Thus the '''cage''' of a stair is the wooden inclosure that encircles it.}}
# {{lb|en|engineering}} A skeleton frame to limit the motion of a loose piece, such as a [[ball valve]].
# A [[wirework]] [[strainer]], used in connection with pumps and pipes.
# {{lb|en|mining}} The [[drum]] on which the rope is wound in a [[hoist]]ing [[whim]].
# {{lb|en|baseball|ice hockey}} The protective [[wire]] [[mask]] at the front of a [[helmet]].
# {{lb|en|graph theory}} A [[regular]] [[graph]] that has as few [[vertex|vertices]] as possible for its [[girth]].
# {{lb|en|killer sudoku}} In [[killer sudoku]] puzzles, a group of connecting cells that must contain a set of unique digits adding up to a certain total, in addition to the usual constraints of sudoku.

